  "note": "Re-judged 2026-11-02 by an independent auditor who authored none of the changes named. RFC 6996 Section 4: \"Private Use ASNs MUST be removed from AS path attributes (including AS4_PATH if utilizing a four-octet AS number space) before being advertised to the global Internet.\" TestRFC6996ExportRemovesPrivateUseASNsFromASPath changed in 76c2b9156a (runEgressPolicyChainASN4 now takes the session facts, passed as policyview.Session{EBGP: true}, matching the EBGP destination the unit already names) and 5c1aea079c (comment spelling). The same four-octet AS_PATH [64511 64512 65534 65535 4199999999 4200000000 4294967294 4294967295] must still come out exactly [64511 65535 4199999999 4294967295] with accept and a wire override, so both edges of both ranges and their neighbours stay pinned. Other carriers byte-identical. Verdict unchanged: enforced.",
